I'm starting today off a little bit  differently it's the last day of  February and this morning I was really  feeling really just kind of down about  the political situation and I know I've  said a bunch of times that I've sort of  become desensitized to the day-to-day of  what's going on stories that sort of  would pretty clearly be major scandals  at some prior point in American history  barely get any attention because it's  sort of scandal after embarrassment  after outrageous scandal day after day  after day and that's still true right  I'm still feeling desensitized to the  day to day but this morning I was really  sort of feeling like the futility of it  all I was thinking about the political  reality right Trump won he's president  he certainly not been able to do  everything he wants but he's doing major  damage to many American institutions  he's really embarrassing the United  States around the world and somehow look  I actually got to a place where I  allowed to creep into my head the idea  and maybe the hatreds whoo right in her  correct that maybe there's nothing more  to really do and the David Pakman show  should kind of like wrap up or come to  an end and I started thinking back you  know the show started when I was in  college sort of on a whim really and  it's grown and grown and it's gone from  something I did after class every other  Wednesday by myself to a five day a week  show with two full-time producers but  are we really having an impact right now  and on a day to day basis I laugh off  the hate reott mails I laugh off the  criticisms that are unhinged and  ridiculous and we have fun with it but  in some way I was wondering like are  they right are they right in some way  are we sort of trying to empty a pool  with a tea spoon sort of an analogy for  an exercise in futility and I've never  believed that it's a waste of time I've  never listened to the haters in a real  way if I had the show would have  probably ended in that basement in  Northampton Massachusetts  w XO J more than ten years ago without  ever having a single employee or dollar  of revenue and it's really easy to  convince oneself that you're having an  impact right like hey we built something  sustainable most independent shows like  this one never even make that single  dollar nevermind being able to have  staff and a private studio but what is  the political impact here right  maybe we failed in some way maybe I  should go back to electronic sales  although I couldn't cuz Circuit City is  out of business or a teaching college or  something and producer Pat can become I  don't know an airline pilot or something  and producer Noah Ferguson could go sell  insurance I don't know why I'm picking  these things but whatever right insert  some other activity and I realized I was  going down this negative path that  really served no purpose so I tried to  reframe and think about it in a  different way and I went back to our  audience email archives which are not  there only in case we ever need to  submit some of those emails as evidence  in a federal trial against someone who  sends us a hundred bizarre emails I also  keep them to be able to see the praise  that we've received then mixed in with  all of the hater messages there were  some really positive messages about how  I influenced this law school student  five years ago to go in the direction of  public defense or Environmental Law or  how that person two years ago had never  really understood why politics even  mattered but because of the show they  became not only regular viewers but also  activists for the progressive idea and  how I reframed at least in my head was  sort of to realize that it's really easy  to look around and feel like we can't  possibly be having an impact because  after all as I mentioned Trump is  president the u.s. is again becoming a  laughingstock around the world the  Florida Senate is putting together a  bill to arm teachers and we're  destroying our planet every single day  with our disregard for what's going on  with the climate  but then I realized I'm sort of ignoring  my own critical thinking which is that  it's really hard to measure negatives  it's really hard to measure the absence  of something and I wondered what would  we be dealing with right now worldwide  were it not for not just the David  Pakman show it's not a delusion of  grandeur but the whole of independent  progressive media and investigative  journalism and critical reporting that  have exposed political and corporate  wrongdoing and challenge the extremist  ideas in interviews and in analyses and  at least made attempts to create I guess  I'd say a more educated and engaged  public through pieces like for example  the critical thinking miniseries which  we're going to start releasing this week  and really it would be the worst  possible time to end the David Pakman  show even though this feeling of  futility I know is shared by at least  some of our audience it would actually  be the worst time so I know that there  are people in the audience that are  feeling hopeless and many are even  saying David he's gonna win re-election  I just don't know if I can stay involved  in politics I don't think I can do  another seven years of this I sort of  feel the same way on a day-to-day basis  but what I came to realize this morning  I was up early as some of you can  imagine how much time did I have to do  all this thinking what I came to realize  this morning is that we actually have to  stay involved now and for me that means  no no don't don't think about hanging it  up instead think about how to double  down and double the size of the show  which is much more difficult right it  would be way easier to say hey you know  what we lost the trumpets one they have  their guy they're spreading their brand  of sort of anti intellectualism and non  diplomacy and we lost and let's go be  insurance salespeople and airline pilots  and college professors or electronic  salesmen or whatever right but remember  Trump won because of seventy seven  thousand votes in three states  he lost the popular vote by three  million votes and he lost the world  which by and large  was on our side for the past eight years  and is by and large still not on Trump's  side as we've seen in poll after poll  after poll and the silver lining here is  that we do have a resurgence in  political activism as a result of this  administration the likes of which we  arguably haven't seen for a long time so  I actually I started in a very dark  place this morning but I'm here to tell  you that I'm recommitting to the growth  of the show not just the sort of slow  steady growth we've seen since Donald  Trump won in November of 2016 but I'm  thinking way bigger because it actually  is the time to grow not the time to walk  away and it's gonna require not only  doing the daily show that we do but  continuing to do the long-form pieces  doing the extras like the critical  thinking miniseries that starts to be  released this week but by the way thanks  to your support and a lot of other  things and if you believe that it's time  to renew the commitment you probably  think I'm gonna say become a member now  but I'm not gonna say that if I mean yes  sure if you value what we do become a  member but if you also think it's time  then help spread the message that there  are alternatives to this sort of  depraved anti intellectual pseudo  jingoistic nonsense that has been  perpetrated by those in the Oval Office  and whether it's emailing shows that you  listen to or watch and say hey maybe  interview David Pakman or emailing me  and say hey interview this other  progressive host or activist who's doing  something great or posting clips to  Facebook or even just tweeting and  emailing in and saying hey David I'm  glad you decided not to walk away  because what you're doing is valuable  and it's a piece of what we all should  be doing and that is doubling down now  and definitely not backing out so my  commitment here is that if there is the  desire and if there is the demand and  the audience infrastructure we're ready  to go sort of full steam ahead now if  the desire isn't there if I'm wrong here  and you're going to hear me say this and  you'll be more influenced by the idea of  walk  away rather than doubling down let me  know say you know what David I think  your initial instinct this morning very  early this morning was the right one  which is we've failed  we've lost there's no coming back and  you might as well walk away because  we're walking away let me know I don't  think that's the case I think I'm going  to hear from people who are going to say  no you know what David in spite of the  feeling of futility in spite of the  questions around what exactly was  accomplished over the last eight years  nine years leading up to Trump's  election if this is where we are now I  think the overwhelming majority in our  audience not the haters but really our  core audience is going to hear this and  they're going to say no no no it's time  to double down and we're here to help  you do that send me your thoughts I'm on  Twitter at D Pakman the show is on  twitter at david pakman show and we're  here we've got a fantastic program for  you today lots of news lots of activism  and lots of new things going on that I'm  going to talk to you right after the  break about
 

